From cfea699fd49ce5579cbdb5c226a66279e10f61ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jared Wyles <jared.wyles@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 10:55:48 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 24/32] ggml-metal: compile a gather-free row-list attention
 variant

When every block of every row list is consecutive or padding, the
host picks a vec pipeline whose gather code is compiled out
(FC_flash_attn_ext_vec_rows_dense): one uniform load per block gives
the base row and the K/V loads are the dense path's. The lists are
host-visible inputs, so the check is a scan of the block ends.

Every Metal buffer type reports is_host false, so the host asks the
buffer's own is_shared whether it may read the lists.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
